# Supabase — Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_or_publishable_key

# Optional — shown on in-app Help & support (mailto link). Example: support@yourdomain.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@example.com

# Site URL — used when reverse proxies hide Host (optional but recommended in production).
# Must match the URL users open in the browser (used for Supabase email redirect links).
# Use the SAME scheme + host as production (e.g. https + www if that is your canonical site).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.maacare.xyz

# --- Supabase Auth → URL configuration (critical for password reset & email links) ---
# If "Site URL" or "Redirect URLs" do not match your app, Supabase sends users to the site root
# with ?code=... only (e.g. https://www.maacare.xyz/?code=...). This app forwards that to
# /auth/callback, but you should still fix Supabase so links use /auth/callback directly.
#
# In Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → URL configuration:
#   - Site URL: your canonical origin, e.g. https://www.maacare.xyz (not http://maacare.xyz if you use HTTPS + www)
#   - Redirect URLs — add every variant you use, for example:
#        https://www.maacare.xyz/auth/callback
#        https://www.maacare.xyz/**
#        http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
#   - Password reset uses resetPasswordForEmail (recovery) and “log in with email code” uses
#     signInWithOtp — both are started from the browser (Supabase JS) so PKCE matches /auth/callback.
#   - Sign up uses browser signUp() for the same reason (confirmation links use PKCE).
#   - The app uses: {origin}/auth/callback?next=... (origin = window.location / request host).
#
# --- Email: one-time code vs link (two different templates) ---
# Forgot password → Dashboard → Email Templates → “Reset password” (recovery). Add {{ .Token }} to
# show the OTP; {{ .ConfirmationURL }} is the reset link. See https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/auth-email-templates
# Log in with email code → “Magic Link” template — same {{ .Token }} / {{ .ConfirmationURL }} rules.

# --- Auth emails (Gmail, etc.) ---
# Password reset, signup confirmation, and email OTP are sent by Supabase Auth — not by this Next.js app.
# To use your personal Gmail:
#   1) Google Account → Security → 2-Step Verification → App passwords → create an app password for "Mail".
#   2) Supabase Dashboard → Project → Authentication → SMTP Settings → Enable custom SMTP
#      Host: smtp.gmail.com  Port: 465 (SSL)  User: your@gmail.com  Pass: (16-char app password)
#      Sender email: your@gmail.com (or your preferred "from" if allowed)

# Required for reliable sign-in / profile creation without manual SQL (service_role secret — never expose to the browser).
# Also used by `npm run import-bd-facilities` (server-side bulk upsert only).
# Admin panel: user role changes, Auth ban/confirm email, and loading other users' pregnancy snippets on community profiles when opted in.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_secret

# Resend — optional; used to email users when an admin applies a ban (see src/lib/email/resend.ts).
# If unset, bans still apply in Supabase Auth but no custom email is sent.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM="MaaCare <noreply@yourdomain.com>"

# Google AI Studio — Gemini chat + embeddings
# Single key, or comma-separated list (tried in order; next key on quota/rate limit).
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key1,key2,key3
GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-004

# Groq fallback when Gemini is exhausted (optional). GROQ_API_KEYS is comma-separated.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEYS=
# GROQ_CHAT_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# Gemini Maps / Places (optional — see src/lib/maps/gemini-maps.ts)
